<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Claim</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>claim dictionary
</pre>
<p>Makes a dictionary yours. A dictionary holds the old kind of aliases, the 
ones that work in any telnet client (see <a cmd='#'>Help Dictionary</a>). You type claim 
once, when you first start using a dictionary; after that it remembers its 
owner. The aliases in a dictionary only work for its owner: anyone else 
who picks it up is told to claim it first.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Dictionary</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Alias</a>
</pre>




</div>